## Pulumi Conventions

### Stack Naming

Always use `<project>/<env>` format:
- `my-infra/dev`, `my-infra/staging`, `my-infra/prod`
- Never use environment names alone (`dev`, `prod`) — they conflict with other projects in the same organization
- Stack names are immutable after creation; choose deliberately

### State Backend

| Environment | Backend | Why |
|-------------|---------|-----|
| Local dev (solo) | `pulumi login --local` | No setup required |
| Shared / CI | Pulumi Cloud | Secrets encryption, concurrency locking, audit log |
| AWS-only, no SaaS | `pulumi login s3://bucket` | S3 backend with DynamoDB lock |
| GCP-only, no SaaS | `pulumi login gs://bucket` | GCS backend with built-in locking |
| Azure-only, no SaaS | `pulumi login azblob://container` | Azure Blob backend |

**Never use local backend for shared environments.** Local state has no concurrency locking — concurrent `pulumi up` runs will corrupt state. Shared teams must use a backend with locking.

### Output/Input Typing

```typescript
// Correct: use .apply() for Output transformations
const connectionUrl = db.endpoint.apply(ep => `postgres://${ep}:5432/mydb`);

// Correct: combine multiple Outputs
const fullArn = pulumi.all([bucket.bucket, bucket.region])
  .apply(([name, region]) => `arn:aws:s3:::${name}`);

// Correct: pulumi.interpolate for string templates with Outputs
const url = pulumi.interpolate`https://${lb.dnsName}/api`;

// Wrong: .get() outside of unit tests
const name = bucket.id.get(); // Only valid with pulumi.runtime.setMocks()
```

### Secrets Configuration

```bash
# Correct: mark config values as secrets (encrypted in state)
pulumi config set --secret databasePassword "hunter2"

# Wrong: plaintext secrets in Pulumi.<stack>.yaml
# config:
#   my-app:databasePassword: hunter2   # NEVER do this
```

Secrets set with `--secret` are encrypted in state using the stack's secrets provider (Pulumi Cloud managed, or a KMS key for self-managed backends).

### Resource Naming

Provide explicit `name` arguments for resources where stable identity matters:

```typescript
// Provides stable name for drift detection and cross-stack references
const bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket("app-assets", {
  bucket: `${pulumi.getProject()}-${pulumi.getStack()}-assets`,
  tags: {
    Environment: pulumi.getStack(),
    Project: pulumi.getProject(),
    ManagedBy: "pulumi",
  },
});
```

Auto-generated names (Pulumi appends random suffix by default) make drift correlation difficult in large stacks.

### CrossGuard Policy Packs

```typescript
import { PolicyPack, validateResourceOfType } from "@pulumi/policy";

new PolicyPack("required-tags", {
  policies: [{
    name: "resources-must-have-env-tag",
    description: "All resources must have an Environment tag",
    enforcementLevel: "mandatory",
    validateResource: (args, reportViolation) => {
      const tags = (args.props as any).tags ?? {};
      if (!tags.Environment) {
        reportViolation("Resource is missing required 'Environment' tag");
      }
    },
  }],
});
```

Run policy packs: `pulumi preview --policy-pack path/to/policy-pack`

### Stack References (Cross-Stack)

```typescript
// Import outputs from another Pulumi stack
const infraStack = new pulumi.StackReference("org/infra/prod");
const vpcId = infraStack.getOutput("vpcId"); // Returns Output<any>
```

Stack references are Pulumi's equivalent of CloudFormation `Fn::ImportValue`. Unlike CFN exports, they do not create deployment ordering constraints — but do create a logical dependency.

### Anti-Patterns

- `pulumi login --local` for team or CI environments — no locking, state corruption risk
- Stack names without project prefix (`dev` instead of `my-infra/dev`) — ambiguous across projects
- Calling `.get()` on Output values in production code — only valid in unit tests with mocked providers
- Storing secrets as plaintext in `Pulumi.<stack>.yaml` — always use `pulumi config set --secret`
- Using default auto-generated resource names in environments where drift detection matters
- Running `pulumi up` without first reviewing `pulumi preview` output in shared environments

### Tooling

| Tool | Command | Purpose |
|------|---------|---------|
| `pulumi preview` | `pulumi preview --diff` | Review planned changes before apply |
| `pulumi up` | `pulumi up --yes` (CI only) | Apply changes |
| `pulumi refresh` | `pulumi refresh` | Sync state with actual cloud resources |
| `pulumi destroy` | `pulumi destroy` | Tear down stack |
| `pulumi config` | `pulumi config set --secret` | Manage stack configuration |

